<PageLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description={`The terms that govern your use of ${SITE.name}.`}
  path="/terms"
  subtitle="The rules for using this site."
  updated={lastUpdated}
>
  <p>
    These terms govern your use of {SITE.url} (the "site"), operated by
    {SITE.legal.entityName} from India. By using the site you agree to them. If you do
    not agree, please do not use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Using the site</h2>

  <p>You may read, link to, quote and share our articles. We ask that you do not:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>republish articles in full without written permission;</li>
    <li>
      scrape the site at a volume that degrades it for other readers, or in a way that
      disregards our <code>robots.txt</code>;
    </li>
    <li>attempt to gain unauthorised access to the site or any related infrastructure;</li>
    <li>
      use the site's content to train a machine-learning model without a separate
      written agreement;
    </li>
    <li>interfere with the advertising that funds the site;</li>
    <li>use the site for any unlawful purpose.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Content ownership</h2>

  <p>
    All articles, images, layout and code on this site are owned by
    {SITE.legal.entityName} or its licensors and are protected by copyright under the
    Indian Copyright Act, 1957 and applicable international treaties. Product names,
    logos and trademarks belong to their respective owners and appear here for
    identification and commentary only, which implies no affiliation or endorsement.
  </p>

  <p>
    Quoting a reasonable extract with clear attribution and a link back is fine and
    encouraged. For anything more — syndication, translation, commercial reuse — email
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.author.email}`}>{SITE.author.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>

  <p>
    The site and its content are provided "as is" and "as available", without warranty
    of any kind, express or implied, including any implied warranty of merchantability,
    fitness for a particular purpose or non-infringement. We do not warrant that the
    site will be uninterrupted, timely, secure or error-free, nor that any article is
    accurate or current.
  </p>

  <p>
    Articles are drafted with AI assistance and reviewed by a person before publishing.
    See the <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a>, which forms part of these terms, for
    what that means and for the limits of the information published here.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>

  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE.legal.entityName} shall not be liable
    for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, or for
    any loss of profits, revenue, data or goodwill, arising out of or in connection
    with your use of or inability to use the site — including any decision you make in
    reliance on anything published here.
  </p>

  <p>
    Nothing in these terms excludes or limits liability where it would be unlawful to
    do so, including liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, or
    for fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation.
  </p>

  <h2>External links and advertising</h2>

  <p>
    Articles link to third-party sites, and the site displays advertising served by
    Google. We do not control that content and are not responsible for it. A link or an
    advertisement is not an endorsement, and any dealings you have with a third party
    are strictly between you and them.
  </p>

  <h2>Indemnity</h2>

  <p>
    You agree to indemnify and hold harmless {SITE.legal.entityName} against any claim
    arising from your misuse of the site or your breach of these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>

  <p>
    We may revise these terms. When we do, we update the revision date shown at the top
    of this page, and — for changes that materially affect your rights — we will note
    the change on the site's front page for a reasonable period. Continuing to use the
    site after a revision constitutes acceptance of it.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>

  <p>
    These terms are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of India,
    without regard to conflict-of-law rules. The courts at
    {SITE.legal.jurisdiction} shall have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute
    arising out of or relating to these terms or the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>

  <p>
    Questions about these terms go to
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.author.email}`}>{SITE.author.email}</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
